where $\Gamma(f_{1},f_{2})$ denotes the collection of all measures on $X\times X$ with first and second marginal respectively equal to $f_{1}$ and $f_{2}$. By the Monge-Kantorovitch duality, the Wasserstein distance of order $1$ can be represented equivalently by the formula
